docs {
  # Get Report By ID (Protected)

  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/reports/:id`
  **Auth:** Required (User or Admin Access Token)

  ## Description
  Retrieves a single report by its ID. Users may only view reports they submitted. Admins may view any report.

  ## Request

  ### Path Parameters

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | `int64` | Yes | Unique ID of the report |

  ### Headers
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`) |

  ## Response
  **`200 OK`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "reporter_user_id": 1,
      "reported_user_id": 2,
      "reason": "HARASSMENT",
      "description": "User is sending offensive and harassing messages repeatedly.",
      "status": "PENDING",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-02T19:00:00Z"
    }
  }
  ```
  ## Errors

  * `400 Bad Request` — Invalid report ID format
  * `401 Unauthorized` — Missing or invalid token
  * `403 Forbidden` — Access denied (report belongs to another user and requester is not admin)
  * `404 Not Found` — Report not found
}
